@page "/guide/transactions"
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Transactions"; }
<div class="docs-layout shell">
    <partial name="_GuideNavigation" />
    <article class="docs-content guide-article">
        <p class="eyebrow">CHAPTER 03</p>
        <h1>Transactions</h1>
        <p class="lead">Every balance change is represented by an entry you can inspect. Choose the correct transaction type so reports remain accurate.</p>

        <h2 id="create">Record an entry</h2>
        <p>Select <strong>New transaction</strong> from the Transactions page or use an account card shortcut on the dashboard. Choose the type first; the form adapts to the information that type needs.</p>
        <figure class="guide-figure">
            <img src="~/images/guide/transaction-form.jpg" alt="New transaction form for an expense with account, amount, category, date and note fields" />
            <figcaption>Categories appear for income and expenses, while transfers ask for a source and target account.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <div class="transaction-types">
            <div><span class="type-dot expense"></span><strong>Expense</strong><p>Reduces one account and contributes to expense reporting.</p></div>
            <div><span class="type-dot income"></span><strong>Income</strong><p>Increases one account and contributes to income reporting.</p></div>
            <div><span class="type-dot transfer"></span><strong>Transfer</strong><p>Moves value between accounts without counting as income or expense.</p></div>
            <div><span class="type-dot adjustment"></span><strong>Adjustment</strong><p>Corrects a balance without describing normal financial activity.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="guide-callout warning"><strong>Transfers across currencies need both amounts.</strong><p>Enter the amount leaving the source account and the amount arriving in the target account. PocketLedger preserves both values instead of inventing an exchange rate.</p></div>

        <h2 id="history">Find and review transactions</h2>
        <p>Filter by year and month, then open <strong>More filters</strong> for account, category, type, amount range or text search. Each day groups its incoming and outgoing totals.</p>
        <figure class="guide-figure">
            <img src="~/images/guide/transactions.jpg" alt="Transaction history grouped by date with monthly filters and categorized entries" />
            <figcaption>The history keeps the category, note, time, account and signed amount visible at a glance.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <p>Select any row to inspect the complete entry. From there you can edit or delete ordinary transactions. Entries generated by debt operations point back to the debt that owns them.</p>
        <figure class="guide-figure">
            <img src="~/images/guide/transaction-details.jpg" alt="Transaction details showing type, amount, account, category, date and note" />
            <figcaption>Details are the safest place to verify an entry before editing it.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <nav class="chapter-pager" aria-label="Chapter navigation"><a asp-page="/Guide/AccountsAndCategories"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> Accounts &amp; categories</a><a asp-page="/Guide/Planning">Planning &amp; insights <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></nav>
    </article>
</div>
